<h2>Common questions</h2>
<h3>When should a Poinciana well be replaced instead of repaired?</h3><p>Replace when casing fails, the well repeatedly pumps sand, yield stays low after pump service, or repair quotes approach half the cost of a new well.</p>
<h3>How deep are wells in Poinciana, FL?</h3><p>Depths vary by location and aquifer target; shallow irrigation wells and deeper household wells differ significantly. A driller confirms depth from nearby well records.</p>
